# Half-Life hand grenade. Measured by vrcardgen, finished by hand.
#
# The model has every bone this needs, and the plan names them: a `ring` that
# turns 1.16 radians in `pinpull`, a `pin` that leaves with it, and a `spoon`
# that owns 7% of the mesh and is never animated - because in Half-Life the
# spoon never moves.
#
# HOW IT WORKS, and why it is not the fuse-from-pin the stock game uses.
#
# The pin does not start anything. It stops the spoon moving before you have
# hold of the grenade, and once it is out your GRIP is what holds the spoon
# down. Let the spoon go - with the thumb, deliberately - and the fuse runs
# while the grenade is still in your hand. That is cooking, and it is a thing
# you choose to do rather than a timer that started behind your back.
#
# Throwing does the same thing without the decision: a hand that opens to
# throw is a hand that has stopped holding the spoon.
#
# One mechanism, both behaviours. Standard fidelity can still force the stock
# fuse-from-pin for players who want it, which is a rule on top of this and
# not a different mechanism underneath.

weapon v_grenade
match  bones 35  seqs 8  hash 0xf991b830

type   thrown
fuse   3500        # Half-Life's, and it starts when the SPOON goes

# The ring. Pulled until the pin is clear of its lugs - measured at 1.16
# radians, which is the whole of the pinpull animation's travel.
joint 0  bone "ring"  hinge  travel 1.16  rest 0
    # A PIN RING HAS NO RETURN SPRING. Stated as an explicit zero rather than
    # left silent: silence means "use the default for this kind of joint", and
    # that default is a pistol slide's return, which climbed the ring back into
    # the fuse the moment the hand came off it.
    spring 0
    point pin_clear at 0.70
    grab  point 0.00 0.00 0.00  radius 2.0

# The spoon. It is held by your grip, not by a catch on a joint, so its
# control names no joint - the one control in the format that does not.
control spoon  at 0.00 0.00 0.00  finger thumb  kind button

# `pin` travels 48 units in the pinpull animation, which is not a mechanism:
# it is the pin being thrown away. The feed path owns it.
#
# `spoon` exists, owns 68 vertices and is never animated. Moving it wants a
# declared travel and an animation written for it by the surgery - which is
# possible today and is not done here, because nobody has measured the arc a
# spoon actually swings through on this model.
